#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
vmux — a picker for Claude Code tmux sessions on a remote machine.

Bare `vmux` always opens the picker, whatever is running.

Creating a session with a blank name gives it a throwaway timestamp name, and a
watcher on the remote machine renames it to match Claude's own session title
once Claude has something to call it.

Attachments survive a closed laptop: when the SSH transport dies, vmux waits
for the host to come back and re-attaches. The tmux session on the remote
machine keeps running the whole time, so a Claude job started before the lid
closed is still going (with its scrollback) when you reattach.

Everything machine-specific — the host, how to start a stopped VM, how to log
in again — lives in a config file written by `vmux setup`.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

